@* M4.S7 — bypass <Router>/<Routes> (which trips an AOT struct-copy bug
   in StaticHtmlRenderer.RenderAttributes when reading reference-typed
   attribute values like NotFoundPage Type / AppAssembly). Render Counter
   inline, same pattern that works in RazorOnIc.canister.wasm. The
   interactive @rendermode handling on Counter still kicks in via the
   inline component reference; blazor.web.js sees the
   <!--Blazor:server--> markers and opens the /_blazor WS regardless. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>Blazor Server on IC — Counter</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body style="font-family: system-ui; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
    <h1 style="color: #2563eb;">Blazor Server on IC</h1>
    <p>Counter rendered server-side, interactivity over IC-WebSocket.</p>

    <Counter />

    <hr />
    <small>Server-rendered shell + <code>blazor.web.js</code> loaded from the asset canister. The shim below rewires <code>window.WebSocket</code> for <code>/_blazor</code> to <code>IcWebSocket</code>.</small>

    <script src="ic-ws-blazor-config.js"></script>
    <script src="ic-websocket.umd.js"></script>
    <script src="ic-ws-blazor-adapter.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
